From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 19:24:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/15] clutter: release input method focus when a focused text
 is destroyed

Actors being destroyed never get key-focus-out, so a ClutterText destroyed
while it had key focus left the input method pointing at it. The next
surrounding text request from the input method, such as after switching
input sources, read the freed text.
---
 clutter/clutter/pango/clutter-text.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/clutter/clutter/pango/clutter-text.c b/clutter/clutter/pango/clutter-text.c
index c7566e30f1e5f801bb1d7737166cf0f3632bdde5..efdd9aeba698ec11b8d47880ea6831a725af9398 100644
--- a/clutter/clutter/pango/clutter-text.c
+++ b/clutter/clutter/pango/clutter-text.c
@@ -1952,6 +1952,9 @@ clutter_text_dispose (GObject *gobject)
 
   g_clear_handle_id (&priv->password_hint_id, mtk_source_remove);
 
+  if (clutter_input_focus_is_focused (priv->input_focus))
+    clutter_input_method_focus_out (clutter_backend_get_input_method (backend));
+
   clutter_text_set_buffer (self, NULL);
   clutter_text_set_input_interceptor (self, NULL);
 
